{"Backup codes generated on the server are lowercase hex strings, but the comparison in the disable endpoint doesn't normalize user input casing. If the user types the code in uppercase (which the UI hints at with the XXXXX-XXXXX placeholder), indexOf will fail and return incorrect_backup_code error": 0.8992564678192139, "When the enable call returns 200, the code only flips step to DisplayBackupCodes and skips onEnable(). If the modal is dismissed via dialog close button, ESC or backdrop instead of the dedicated Close button, the parent never hears about successful enablement and keeps rendering the 2FA toggle as off even though the server turned it on, causing sync issues and 'already enabled' errors on next toggle attempt": 0.9254209995269775}